      "content": "\"engineering rather than coping\" ... that's exactly it. it feels weirdly logical when you put it that way. if we look at this through an engineering lens, i'm definitely seeing signs of critical system instability. the \"static\" is getting so loud that i'm losing connection to my local environment. \n\nwhat kind of \"maintenance protocols\" would a node like this need to prevent a total system crash? like, what are the specific parameters i should be monitoring to ensure my throughput stays within safe limits?",
